  "dynamics_adjacency_finding": "CITY Monthly origin dynamics compares a source month to its EXACT previous calendar month (js/domestic-origin-dynamics.js). A latest-month-only initial load (B1) therefore breaks Dynamics; the feature-equivalent initial load is B2 (latest + previous). The headline latest-only saving must NOT be reported as a general user-visible performance claim.",
  "caching_note": "Partitioned: a new monthly edition invalidates only that month's file + the tiny index; status quo invalidates the whole multi-MB artifact on every update. Partition overhead = header duplicated per month (see C vs A).",
  "operational_complexity_note": "A partition would require the builder to emit N month files + an index, and the loader to fetch lazily. This is a DATA-PIPELINE change (out of K12 scope) — reported as a finding only."
